      "math_academy_id": "q-224994",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(7)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0009\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =0.3007.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
